# The root .gitignore's bare `runs/` matches at any depth, so it swallows this whole tree --
# which is 6.0 GB, almost all of it model checkpoints.
#
# The evidence is worth committing and the artifacts are not: every number in docs/ is
# traceable to a JSON or a log (10 MB together), while the checkpoints (5.9 GB), demo HDF5s
# (158 MB) and videos (34 MB) are all regenerable from the scripts and the recorded seeds.
#
# `runs/*` re-excludes the contents, including the subdirectories, so git never descends into
# them; the two negations then pull back the flat evidence files.
!runs/
runs/*
!runs/*.json
!runs/*.log
